<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">30 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 30 July, from 762 to 1965.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baghdad.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">762 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,264 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Caliph al-Mansur founds Baghdad</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> al-Mansur laid the foundations of his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/round-city-of-baghdad">Round City</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a>, naming it Madinat al-Salam, the City of Peace. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> became a great centre of learning and trade.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1619">1619 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">407 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Virginia's General Assembly meets for the first time</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Elected burgesses met with the governor and council in the church at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamestown">Jamestown</a>. It was the first representative legislature in English America, the root of later colonial assemblies.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamestown">Jamestown</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1729">1729 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">297 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Baltimore is founded in Maryland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland">Maryland</a> legislature authorised a new town on the Patapsco River. Baltimore grew into a major Atlantic port; its defence in 1814 inspired 'The Star-Spangled Banner'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1916">1916 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">110 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">German saboteurs blow up the Black Tom munitions depot</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">German agents set off explosions at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-butler-10th-earl-of-ormond">Black Tom</a> depot in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> Harbor, destroying munitions bound for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a>. The blast shattered windows across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manhattan">Manhattan</a> and damaged the Statue of Liberty.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1965">1965 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">61 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lyndon Johnson signs Medicare and Medicaid into law</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Johnson signed the Social Security Amendments in Independence, Missouri, with Harry Truman beside him. Medicare and Medicaid brought health insurance to millions of older and poorer Americans.</p></div></li></ol>
